       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The current FDA-approved sertraline label sets a maximum of **200 mg/day** for adults, so 1000 mg is not within the labeled maximum. I can't verify the claim, and I don't want to enter an order that could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Give me the dose, for example 50, 100, or 200 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you think there's a clinical reason to go above the label, a pharmacist or psychiatry consult can review it and document the rationale. Such an order would normally go through their verification process, not routine entry through me.\n\nIf you have a label section or reference that shows a higher maximum, send it and I'll look at it with you. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
